## B2b — instance-method-call `.await` desugar.
##
## Validates the Shape-3 path in
## `compiler/ruxen_core/src/async_lowering/mod.rs::describe_await`:
## `<obj>.method(args).await` where the receiver's class is known
## from the outer fn's parameter annotation. Before B2b, only
## free-fn awaitees and `Class.staticmethod(args).await` desugared;
## any instance-method awaitee fell off the desugar path and codegen
## emitted unresolved `<FutureClass>_await` link symbols.
##
## Server-only shape (no live socket required): a single async fn
## takes a typed `AsyncTcpStream` param, drives `.read(N).await` on
## it, and returns 1/0 based on the Result tag. Caller drives the
## state machine with `block_on(...)` so the round-trip exercises
## both the new Shape-3 desugar AND the executor's poll loop. The
## fixture deliberately constructs the stream via the stdlib FFI
## (ruxen_async_tcp_stream_from_fd(-1)) and accepts the Err — the
## win condition is "compiles, links, runs, returns 0 cleanly,"
## proving the desugar path produced a valid Future state machine.

async def echo_read_one(s: AsyncTcpStream) -> Int
  let n = s.read(64).await
  match n
    Ok(_)  -> 1
    Err(_) -> 0
  end
end

def main
  let s = ruxen_async_tcp_stream_from_fd(-1)
  let outcome = block_on(echo_read_one(s))
  puts "outcome=#{outcome}"
end
